- [ ] Bundle client and server together into only one program + one header file?

### Shared
- [ ] Add a define for ICMP_STRUCT_SIZE when size choice is stable
- [ ] Add a function that will send the icmp packet itself, as now server and client send data in multiple places we could refacto to use a function
- [ ] Add some other kind of validation of the packet data, maybe my own checksum - nounce?
- [x] Now we have calculate_checksum that is needed in the client as well to send the ping to the server
- [ ] On both server & client we have smth like this remove (icmp_reply->icmp_type == ICMP_ECHO_REPLY as its in both if clauses) if (icmp_reply->icmp_type == ICMP_ECHO_REPLY && icmp_reply->action == 0)

### Client
- [x] Use poll() to handle concurrent stdin + socket reads simultaneously
- [ ] Add IP address validation on connect
- [ ] Add message buffer split: if msg > 100 chars, send remainder in next packet
      instead of losing data
- [ ] Fix terminal scramble when a message arrives while user is typing
- [ ] Handle Ctrl+C: graceful disconnect from server <- send disconnect package?
- [ ] Move recv buffer allocation outside the while loop (avoid re-init cost)
- [ ] Handle PING from server: reply PONG (ICMP_ECHO_REPLY), do not print to screen

### Server
- [ ] Add max rooms limit to prevent OOM/DDoS via room creation <- For when users can create room
- [ ] Add overflow protection on roomname (> 10 chars overflows) <- For when users can create room
- [ ] Implement cleanup(): remove stale users (last_seen > 10s)
- [ ] Implement send_all_pings() called every ~5 seconds
- [ ] Re-zero recv buffer after each recvfrom to avoid stale data bleed
- [ ] Add packet validation / checksum to identify packets coming from our clients
      (e.g. use icmp_header->padding as a nonce/signature)
- [ ] Fix echo loop: server catches its own ICMP echo, not the reply from client
- [ ] Handle PONG reply from client (update last_seen, do not broadcast)

### Ping/Pong
- [ ] Solve kernel intercepting ICMP echo replies before client app sees them
      Options: use custom ICMP type, or disable kernel ping on client machine too


